    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d9">

                <pb facs="0015" n="7" sameAs="frus:frus1939v02/pg7"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.014 Antarctic/198</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by Mr. Hugh S. Cumming, Jr., of the
                        Division of European Affairs</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-07-18">July 18, 1939</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Dr. Gruening telephoned me today and said that he had received a memorandum from
                    the President directing that American activities <pb facs="0016" n="8"
                        xml:id="pg8"/> in the Antarctic be known as “The United States Antarctic
                    Service”.</p>
                <p>The President preferred not to use the word “Expedition” since that contemplated
                    a more or less temporary rather than permanent interest on the part of the
                    United States in the Antarctic.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
